&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred locations are London, Berlin, Frankfurt, Munich and Hanover; with domestic and occasional international travel as required.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driven by the rapid digital transformation of businesses across Europe, demand for high-capacity, reliable connectivity from Enterprise customers continues to grow. Thanks to our continued investment in the development of European fibre networks, euNetworks is a leader in Data Centre to Data Centre connectivity, supporting Hyperscale, Enterprise, Content and Wholesale customers across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Sales Director Data Centres you will play a key role in driving new business growth across the Enterprise market. You will do this by partnering, &#39;selling with&#39; with the sales teams of our DC customers to develop connectivity solutions for their DC tenants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in an experienced team, you will have the opportunity to develop and close large-scale European network opportunities (100G/400G) with Enterprise organisations that require high-performance connectivity across multiple locations. While you will also support the development of a small number of existing accounts, the primary focus of this role is building pipeline, acquiring new logos and expanding euNetworks’ presence within the Enterprise sector.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the support of our Sales Engineering team, with multiple engineers and additional account support available. You will also work closely with our Network Development, Digital Enablement and Product teams to shape solutions that meet customer needs and drive successful outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will you be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, target and win new Enterprise customers, building a strong pipeline of opportunities across the Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute new business sales strategies to expand euNetworks’ presence in the Enterprise market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders within prospective customer organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive opportunities from initial engagement through contract signature, meeting or exceeding sales and revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a strong understanding of the Enterprise connectivity market, identifying trends, potential customers and new opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Network at industry events, customer meetings and campaigns to generate leads and strengthen euNetworks’ market presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Sales Engineering and Product teams to develop technically and commercially viable solutions for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with commercial and finance teams to develop strong business cases and proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and growth of selected existing accounts, identifying opportunities for upselling and cross-selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage sales activity and pipeline through Salesforce.com, ensuring accurate reporting and data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we want from you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant sales experience within Telecoms, Connectivity, Infrastructure or Technology markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong new business development experience, with a proven ability to generate pipeline and win new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of meeting or exceeding sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling connectivity, network infrastructure or data centre solutions to Enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial mindset, with the drive to identify opportunities and develop new relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, negotiation and relationship-building skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex sales cycles and multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organisational skills and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who is comfortable prospecting and building opportunities from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of the European Telecoms and Enterprise connectivity market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this position is of interest but you don’t think you meet all of the criteria listed, please consider applying still. euNetworks looks to recruit people with the right attitude, potential and ambition and for the right candidate, we will provide further training and support to enable you to develop in the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What can we offer you?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;At euNetworks we invest in our people by offering a range of benefits and development opportunities designed to support your professional growth and personal wellbeing. Employees have access to a comprehensive wellbeing programme that promotes mental health and also recognises the importance of work-life balance through initiatives such as a dedicated birthday day off and “give back” days to support volunteering activities. euNetworks’ bonus scheme is linked to both individual contribution and overall company performance with opportunity to overachieve in both areas. In addition, euNetworks operates a flexible hybrid working policy, enabling employees to balance in-office collaboration with remote work, fostering productivity, autonomy and a positive employee experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Family Friendly Policy delivers enhanced and inclusive parental benefits that can viewed &lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1yM2VvLsByNiULKnRX9pIksCK0GI6FmO2/edit?usp=sharing&amp;amp;ouid=105588911760161167743&amp;amp;rtpof=true&amp;amp;sd=true&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Insurances, pensions, leave and additional enhancements are modelled to work with local country provisions, please email &lt;a ---------- for more details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our company values drive our behaviour and form the basis of how we operate our business. We work as a team promoting a culture of collaboration, trust and respect where every individual is heard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to be an equal opportunity employer and commit to providing each individual with the support, continued learning and the tools to achieve their goals and an environment in which they can thrive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strive to make the hiring process equitable and accessible for all. Providing candidates with the opportunity to be their true selves and explore how you might thrive at euNetworks. We are a recognised Disability Confident employer and will make provisions where possible to support you through the interview process, if you require any reasonable accommodation through the selection process, please let your Talent Partner know.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What do we do?&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;euNetworks is a pan-European provider of bandwidth infrastructure services and a vital enabler of Cloud and AI adoption. We’re the leading connectivity partner for data centre companies and their customers in Europe, directly connecting over 600 data centres today. We own and operate 18 metropolitan city networks connected with a high capacity intercity backbone covering 53 cities in 17 countries. A leading provider of cloud connectivity, we&amp;nbsp;directly connect to all major cloud platforms.&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fireblocks is the company bringing global finance onchain. Backed by over $1 billion in capital, we are the premier digital asset infrastructure provider trusted by thousands of industry-defining financial institutions, including banks, payment providers, fintechs, and global corporates such as BNY Mellon, BNP Paribas, ANZ Bank, Western Union, Stripe, and Revolut. Built for institutional scale and security, our enterprise-grade platform and network have powered over $14 trillion in digital asset transfers worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fireblocks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;, the industry-leading digital asset infrastructure technology company responsible for 15% of all crypto transactions!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s the bit about us:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fireblocks is an enterprise-grade platform delivering a secure infrastructure for moving, storing, and issuing digital assets &amp;amp; cryptocurrencies. At Fireblocks, we enable businesses to securely build, run and scale digital asset operations through the Fireblocks Network and MPC-based Wallet Infrastructure. Our next-generation multi-layer technology protects Digital assets from cyber-attacks, internal collusion, and human error. Fireblocks is the only platform that provides insurance for digital assets in storage, transfer, and E&amp;amp;O.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As of January 2026, we serve over 2400 institutional customers, have secured the transfer of over $10&amp;nbsp;trillion in digital assets, and are the world&#39;s highest-valued digital asset infrastructure company, with over&amp;nbsp;$1 billion raised.&amp;nbsp;Our mission is simple: Enable every business to easily and securely support digital assets &amp;amp;&amp;nbsp;cryptocurrencies. Come join us as we Secure. Simplify. Scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s the bit about the opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Joining the EMEA Fireblocks sales team, you will drive growth for Fireblocks within blockchain payments sector in the DACH region. As a key member of a leading blockchain and cybersecurity firm, you will target PSP, Cross-Border, Remittances and various other payment providers whilst collaborating closely with regional sales teams, Sales Engineers, and the Payments product team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meeting and exceeding monthly and quarterly revenue targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with the Fireblocks BDR and GTM teams to generate and qualify leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and nurturing strong relationships with prospects and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting prospecting, territory, and account planning to identify new opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping the Fireblocks CRM up-to-date with accurate account and pipeline information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise SaaS or institutional sales experience, selling into the Payments space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for blockchain technology and cryptocurrency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within financial services, cybersecurity, or cryptocurrency is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in formalising and supporting the co-sell motion in working with technology partners&amp;nbsp;is preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of over-achievement in an enterprise sales position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial and relentless hunting attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to prospect and qualify for new opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a team-selling environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a comprehensive onboarding and training program for all new employees. We are looking for A players who want to work with the best. Track record of success and closing complex deals within the&amp;nbsp;financial services or fintech sectors&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For employees hired to work from the EU, Fireblocks is required by law to include a reasonable estimate of the compensation range for this role. This range is specific to&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Germany and takes into consideration a wide range of factors that are reviewed when making a hiring decision, such as years of experience, skills, and other business needs. It is not typical for a candidate to be hired at or near the top of the pay range and each compensation decision is dependent on each individual case. A reasonable base salary range estimate for this position is&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;€80,400 – €100,500.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary is one component of the total compensation package, which for some roles may include a target bonus, a very competitive equity grant, and very generous benefits.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;While we believe competitive compensation is a critical aspect of your decision to join us, we do hope you also spend time considering why our mission and culture are right for you. We are creating something transformational here, and we hope you are as excited about the future as we are.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fireblocks&#39; mission is to enable every business to easily and securely access digital assets and cryptocurrencies. In order to do that, we strongly believe&amp;nbsp;our workforce should be as diverse as our clients, and this is why we&amp;nbsp;embrace diversity and inclusion in all its forms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.fireblocks.com/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Please see our candidate privacy policy here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;/div&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

&lt;p&gt;Du willst keinen Job, in dem du nur Skripte vorliest und Tickets weiterreichst. Du willst verstehen, warum ein Prozess klemmt – und ihn wirklich lösen. Als Supporter bei Alpha Online bist du erste Anlaufstelle für Autohäuser, die mit dem AlphaController ihr Tagesgeschäft steuern: von der Gebrauchtfahrzeug-Bewertung bis zum Verkauf.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standort:&lt;/strong&gt; Hamburg – flexibles Homeoffice möglich.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Über uns&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpha Online entwickelt die Prozessmanagement-Software für den professionellen Gebrauchtwagenhandel in Deutschland. Unser Kernprodukt AlphaController steuert alle Arbeitsprozesse im Autohaus – von der Fahrzeugbewertung bis zum Verkauf. Zu unseren Kunden zählen Mercedes-Benz, BMW, Volkswagen, Porsche und Audi. Seit 2024 sind wir Teil von CarOnSale, dem KI-gestützten Betriebssystem für den B2B-Gebrauchtwagenhandel in Europa.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One Platform. One Profit Engine.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Deine Aufgaben&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du bist erste Ansprechperson für unsere Kunden am Telefon und im E-Mail-Postfach – 1st Level mit Perspektive auf 2nd Level – und behältst den administrativen Überblick über alle laufenden Fälle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du konfigurierst den AlphaController passgenau auf die Anforderungen jedes Kunden – von Feature-Freischaltung bis Berechtigungsstruktur&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du analysierst Abhängigkeiten und Fehlerquellen in der Software, bevor sie zum Problem für den Kunden werden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Du testest jedes Release manuell auf Herz und Nieren und steuerst Tickets ein, damit nur fehlerfreie Software beim Kunden ankommt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bei Fehlern an der Schnittstelle zu unseren Partnern gehst du der Ursache auf den Grund, kommunizierst direkt mit Schnittstellenpartnern und interner Entwicklung und trägst zur Behebung bei&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Was du mitbringst&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindestens drei Jahre Erfahrung im direkten Kundenkontakt oder Support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technisches Verständnis für komplexe Softwareprozesse und Schnittstellen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytische, strukturierte Arbeitsweise – du erkennst Abhängigkeiten, bevor sie zum Problem werden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Freude an direktem Kundenkontakt und daran, für jeden Kunden die passende Lösung zu finden&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deutsch auf C2-Niveau, Englisch mindestens B2 in Wort und Schrift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Von Vorteil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erfahrung im Automotive-Sektor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ausbildung im IT-/Software-Bereich, z. B. als Fachinformatiker:in&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Was dich bei uns erwartet&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unbefristete Festanstellung in Hamburgs bester Lage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibles Homeoffice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ein Umfeld, in dem KI und Digitalisierung echte Rolle spielen – kein Lippenbekenntnis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erfahrenes Team mit kurzen Entscheidungswegen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attraktive Vergütung mit Mitarbeiter-Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bewirb dich jetzt – dein Lebenslauf reicht.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Mehr Informationen findest Du auf der Website:&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.alphaonline.de/&quot;&gt; Alpha Online GmbH&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow

